.TH CHECK_FIRMWARE_VERSION.SH 1 "2026-10-06" "otsdaq-mu2e 11.03.00" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
check_firmware_version.sh \- compare the firmware version register of PCIe
devices 0 and 1 with an expected value
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B check_firmware_version.sh
.I expected
.SH DESCRIPTION
The script sources
.I /mu2e/spack_pcie/setup\-env.sh
and runs
.BR "spack env activate pcie" .
It then reads register
.B 0x9004
from PCIe devices 0 and 1 with
.BR "my_cntl \-d0 read 0x9004" " and " "my_cntl \-d1 read 0x9004" .
.BR reset_PCIe_AL9.sh (1)
prints the same register after a reset.
.PP
Each result is the first output line, stdout or stderr, that contains
.BR 0x .
It is compared with
.I expected
as an exact string.
For each device the script prints one line:
.PP
.EX
===> HOST DTC0 Exact version match. *
===> HOST DTC1 Version mismatch! \-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-> <read> and expected <expected>
.EE
.PP
It reads registers only and changes nothing.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.I expected
The register value as
.B my_cntl
prints it, for example
.BR 0xd5100695 .
The comparison is string equality, so case and leading zeros must match.
Exactly one argument is required.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /mu2e/spack_pcie/setup\-env.sh
Spack environment that provides
.B my_cntl
(mu2e-pcie-utils).
This is a different mechanism from the
.I /root/setup_pcie_AL9.sh
that
.BR reset_PCIe_AL9.sh (1)
uses.
.TP
.I /dev/mu2e0 ", " /dev/mu2e1
The devices read.
Only indices 0 and 1 are checked.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B HOSTNAME
Used in messages.
If it is unset, the output of
.B hostname \-f
is used.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 1
Wrong number of arguments.
.TP
.B 0
Every other case, including a mismatch and a missing device.
A missing device gives an empty or error string and is reported as a
mismatch.
To use the result in a script, filter the output for
.BR mismatch .
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
tools/check_firmware_version.sh 0xd5100695
.EE
.PP
Calorimeter nodes, printing only failures:
.PP
.EX
for node in calo\-{01..12} calo\-14; do
    ssh mu2eshift@mu2e\-$node \e
        /path/to/otsdaq\-mu2e/tools/check_firmware_version.sh 0xd5100695
done | grep \-i mismatch
.EE
.PP
The expected value for each firmware build is listed on the daq-operations
wiki page "Firmware-Versions".
